<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-19T15:46:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ebola: Kenya cases rise to 8, spreads to 8th Congo province</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a68bc46debb2863cbc1b92fd3e7b2589703c2248b2207cba26b7b1b6d784cd50</id><updated>2026-10-19T15:44:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T22:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-kenya-cases-rise-to-8-spreads-to-8th-congo-province/a-79694614--896ed853a955.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-kenya-cases-rise-to-8-spreads-to-8th-congo-province/a-79694614?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A senior health official in Kenya said there have now been eight Ebola infections in the country, while in DR Congo the disease has spread to an eighth province.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The Bundestag has debated the genocide Germany carried out in Namibia a century ago. But will it spur progress on addressing colonial crimes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c477e34308c700faf0daf5d419a9d9bf68c7d190824ad5c55afdacb0d9efc41c</id><updated>2026-10-19T15:44:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur/a-79682388--50aa326f1793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur-progress-on-addressing-colonial-crimes/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How prepared is Kenya for an Ebola outbreak?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c698796884b192d1d956ae33294a8b5c8ad8486b9a95ac8c5eaf71ca758e3c6e</id><updated>2026-10-19T15:45:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144--2b6e19c28555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first two confirmed Ebola cases in Kenya have raised urgent questions about the country's public health preparedness and border controls. But the Health Ministry says there is no need for panic.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: DR Congo outbreak not slowing, MSF warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e51ae5e0b8b6c3f8d92748e49338b4650c0a85e61bea65bd0ffb89decaf073d7</id><updated>2026-10-19T15:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719--f40efdc02bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors Without Borders has warned against premature optimism amid the DRC's largest-ever Ebola outbreak. "The outbreak is not shrinking, it is moving," an MSF official said, entering new and more underprepared regions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
